                <person xml:id="MAC20" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Maitland</forename>
                        <surname>Mackintosh</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1796-06-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1861"/>
                    <occupation>Daughter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> This identification is tentative. It is possible that Mackintosh JR
                            refers to either of Sir James Mackintosh's daughters, Mary or Maitland,
                            however owing to the timing of the entry it is more likely that the
                            entry refers to Maitland. Her relationship witb Godwin is unclear given
                            her father's political beliefs, however given the fact that she is only
                            referenced once in the diary it should be assumed that they were not
                            close.</p>
                    </note>
